{
  "_comment": "The rules of a vehicle's tyre history (#287): a swap, a change of positions and the checks every change passes, read by the server (Domain TyreSwapContractTests, over TyreHistory) and by the device (frontend TyreHistory.unit, over src/tyres/tyreHistory.ts), so a tyre change made offline shows as the server will make it. 'new' is the id of the installation an operation creates; 'expect' lists the live installations after it, by first day; 'error' is the refusal, its key and its args; 'move' moves the swap that began an installation to another day (its line's day changed, #288); 'lines' lists the tyre log's live lines after it, by day (every installation has its line, with its id: a change of positions when the same set came off that day, else a swap; 'kept' is a Note line that keeps what a line held for a day a join took its installation away from), 'trashedLines' the lines that went to the trash, 'lineNotes' the notes on the lines before; 'moving' lists the installations a check is about (added, edited or restored), so an overlap names the other one.",
